{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/lineBreak"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/plain(_:)"],"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextWrap"}],"symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextWrap"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:6Gnusto8TextWrapO","title":"TextWrap","role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Renders game prose for a channel: reflowed to a column width for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full-screen terminal, folded for every plain one. Pure and side-effect-free"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it can be unit-tested without a live terminal."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextWrap","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The whole transcript is re-wrapped at the current width on every render, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this is the one place the “smart reflow on resize” behavior actually lives.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text is treated by Markdown’s paragraph rule: a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"single","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" newline inside a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paragraph is a soft break that folds to a space, and only a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"blank line"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts a new paragraph. Game prose is authored as multi-line ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\"\""},{"text":" literals","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrapped for source readability, so honoring those incidental newlines as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hard breaks would shatter the layout whenever the window is narrower than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the width the author happened to wrap at (dangling “This”, “and”, …).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Folding them makes the layout depend on the channel and never on the column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the author happened to type at."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" channels apply that rule, which is the whole point of this type."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They used to disagree: the reflowing one folded and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/plain(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" did not,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a literal printed at the source’s wrap column on the one channel that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcripts, CI and every play-test artifact are read in — and at "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"two"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"columns the moment a clause was concatenated onto it. That is what made a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trailing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\"},{"type":"text","text":" on every prose line look like a convention. It never was one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it was a workaround for this, and there is nothing left for it to work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"around."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Three ways to say something other than “this is running prose”:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"blank line","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" starts a new paragraph.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/lineBreak","type":"reference"},{"text":" marker ","type":"text"},{"code":"<br>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a hard break "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"within","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a paragraph, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a banner’s title over its tagline. Non-whitespace, so unlike a trailing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"double space it survives editors and formatters that trim line endings."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Indentation"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" makes a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"form"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": an inscription, a map legend, a ring of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"letters cut round a shaft, a scrap of verse. Both channels read it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Markdown reads it — a literal block, never folded and never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"re-packed. That is a description of what this package’s authors already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"did, not a rule imposed on them: every such block in every game target is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indented, and nothing else in a game target is.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One internal "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fold"},{"type":"text","text":" is the single implementation of all of that, and both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/plain(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the reflowing renderer are built on it, so the two channels"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot drift apart again about what a paragraph is.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/plain(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/lineBreak","type":"reference"},{"text":" are public: a front end that prints text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"needs to render the marker and the fold, and the terminal-column machinery","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behind the full-screen handler is the engine’s own.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/textwrap"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TextWrap/plain(_:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plain","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Renders game text for a plain, non-reflowing channel: folds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paragraph’s soft breaks, then turns the hard-break marker into a real","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newline.","type":"text"}],"title":"plain(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/plain(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/textwrap\/plain(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TextWrap/lineBreak":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lineBreak"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The in-band hard line-break marker (as in Markdown\/HTML): a break within","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a paragraph, no blank line, formatter-proof. The full-screen renderer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"honors it through the fold; plain output turns it into a newline via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/plain(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" so it never shows literally.","type":"text"}],"title":"lineBreak","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/textwrap\/linebreak","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap\/lineBreak"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TextWrap":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextWrap"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextWrap"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Renders game prose for a channel: reflowed to a column width for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full-screen terminal, folded for every plain one. Pure and side-effect-free"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it can be unit-tested without a live terminal."}],"title":"TextWrap","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/textwrap","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextWrap"}}}